# Playwright-tools scope

This package is shared across **all** ComponentK Shopware plugins. Do not bind helpers to one plugin.

## Plugin-agnostic only

- No plugin-specific store keys, snippet keys, test IDs, CSS classes, or route names in exported APIs.
- No constants like `ckou.afu.*`, `ckou-vdocs-*`, or AFU/ACAF/VDOCS fixture names in services or `adminUi.ts`.
- Generic flow/customer/cart helpers are fine; **plugin overrides** belong in that plugin's `tests/fixtures/`.

## Where plugin-specific test code lives

| Concern | Location |
|---------|----------|
| AFU flow list filter store key, sidebar assertions | `CKOUAdvFlowUtility/tests/fixtures/flowList.ts` |
| VDOCS customer tab navigation | VDOCS plugin fixtures (or generic customer helpers here) |
| Shared admin hash nav, flow row locator, `gotoFlowIndexReady` | playwright-tools `adminUi.ts` |

## Extract vs keep local

Extract to playwright-tools when **two or more plugins** need the same pattern and it stays generic (e.g. `gotoFlowIndexReady`, `flowListRow`, `AdminApi.resetUserConfigKey`).

Keep in the plugin when the helper references plugin UI overrides, test IDs, or config keys.

## Debugging / verification runs

When fixing one spec or feature, run **only that file or test name** — not the full `@single-worker` or `@admin` project:

```bash
cd custom/plugins/<Plugin>/tests
pnpm exec playwright test -c playwright.config.ts --project chromium path/to/spec.ts --workers 1
pnpm exec playwright test -c playwright.config.ts --grep "exact test title" --workers 1
```

Rebuild admin JS only when administration sources changed; then rerun the targeted spec.
